WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
Every second, your body makes
about four million new cells.

2
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.640
Each one needs a complete
set of chromosomes.

3
00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:08.900
Not most of them.

4
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.070
All of them.

5
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.190
And the parent cell doesn't
survive as a third cell.

6
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.000
Its contents are shared out between two.

7
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:20.360
So how does each new cell end up
with a full set of chromosomes?

8
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.960
In this mission, you'll name
the four stages of mitosis,

9
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:26.560
and see what the spindle does in each.

10
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.580
Then you'll see why a plant cell
can't simply be pinched in two,

11
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.750
and what it builds instead.

12
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.350
Your mission: find out how every new cell
ends up with a complete set of chromosomes.
